        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.189,
            0.187,
            0.407,
            0.205
          ],
          "content": "Difference = 10,22,447"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.245,
            0.883,
            0.322
          ],
          "content": "**10.You are given some number cards; 4000, 13000, 300, 70000, 150000, 20, 5. Using the cards get as close as you can to the numbers below using any operation you want. Each card can be used only once for making a particular number.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.323,
            0.623,
            0.342
          ],
          "content": "**(a) 1,10,000:** 4000 × (20 + 5) + 13000 = 1,13,000"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.356,
            0.819,
            0.396
          ],
          "content": "**(b) 2,00,000: Ans:** closest estimate = 1,50,000 + 70,000 – (4000 × 5) = 2,00,000."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.415,
            0.783,
            0.454
          ],
          "content": "**(c) 5,80,000: Ans:** closest estimate = (1,50,000 × 4) – (4000 × 5) = 5,80,000."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.177,
            0.474,
            0.8,
            0.552
          ],
          "content": "**(d) 12,45,000: Ans:** closest estimate = (70,000 × 20) – 1,50,000 – 4,000 – (300 × 5) = 12,44,500."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.572,
            0.846,
            0.611
          ],
          "content": "**(e) 20,90,800: Ans:** closest estimate = (1,50,000 × 14) + 4,000 – 13,000 = 20,91,000."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.63,
            0.881,
            0.669
          ],
          "content": "**11.Find out how many coins should be stacked to match the height of the Statue of Unity. Assume each coin is 1 mm thick.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.67,
            0.855,
            0.748
          ],
          "content": "**Ans:** Height of each coin = 1 mm Height of Statue of Unity = 180 m = 180 × 100 × 10 mm = 1, 80,000 mm. Number of coins to be stacked = 1,80,000 mm ÷ 1 mm = 1,80,000 coins."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.767,
            0.884,
            0.865
          ],
          "content": "**12.Grey-headed Albatrosses have a roughly 7-feet wide wingspan. They are known to migrate across several oceans. Albatrosses can cover about 900 – 1000 km in a day. One of the longest single trips recorded is about 12,000 km. How many days would such a trip take to cross an ocean approximately?**"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
